# Typing over a selection then one Ctrl+Z restores the selected text, as
# VS Code (and the Rust app) do: the replaced selection and the typed run
# are one undo stop. The run's first char claimed it without naming its
# owner, so the second char opened a group of its own and Ctrl+Z left
# "X" behind (round-7 hunt). Both faces: one selection, and two Ctrl+D
# selections.
write a.txt "abc def\n"
write b.txt "foo bar foo\n"
open a.txt
key shift+end
type XY
key ctrl+z
expect screen contains "1 abc def"
key ctrl+s
expect file a.txt contains "abc def\n"
open b.txt
key ctrl+d
key ctrl+d
type XY
key ctrl+s
expect file b.txt contains "XY bar XY"
key ctrl+z
key ctrl+s
expect file b.txt contains "foo bar foo\n"
